// ATT&CK: execution, stealth
// Tags: detection.threat-hunting
// Description: Detects child processes of "dfsvc" which indicates a ClickOnce deployment execution.
// False positives:
//   - False positives are expected in environement leveraging ClickOnce deployments. An initial baselining is required before using this rule in production.
// References:
//   - https://posts.specterops.io/less-smartscreen-more-caffeine-ab-using-clickonce-for-trusted-code-execution-1446ea8051c5
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/68e86efccf6969a2175f7e6c280cde81b1ae8eea/rules-threat-hunting/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_dfsvc_child_processes.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\dfsvc.exe" and FolderPath contains "\\AppData\\Local\\Apps\\2.0\\"
